From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipc: write a call's whole reply, and say when one is lost

A call's connection was deleted on the next turn of the event loop,
straight after its reply was handed to the socket. Deleting a local
socket aborts it, so a reply longer than the socket's buffer, about
100,000 characters, was cut off, and `qs ipc call` printed only
"QLocalSocket::PeerClosedError". A shell listing what it holds, such
as a launcher's catalogue, couldn't answer. And qs exited 0 all the
same, since the client threw away what each command returned, so a
script couldn't tell a lost reply, or any failed call, from one that
came.

A connection that isn't kept for a signal now disconnects from its
client, which writes what's pending before it closes, and is deleted
when the disconnect lands, as a client's own disconnect already
deleted it. The client exits with what its command returned.

---
diff --git a/src/ipc/ipc.cpp b/src/ipc/ipc.cpp
index 9a47c50..04c60d3 100644
--- a/src/ipc/ipc.cpp
+++ b/src/ipc/ipc.cpp
@@ -87,9 +87,11 @@ void IpcServerConnection::onReadyRead() {
 
 	if (!this->stream.commitTransaction()) return;
 
-	// async connections reparent
+	// async connections reparent. The rest close once their reply is written,
+	// and onDisconnected deletes them: deleting the socket at once would drop
+	// whatever of a long reply the socket's buffer couldn't take yet.
 	if (dynamic_cast<IpcServer*>(this->parent()) != nullptr) {
-		this->deleteLater();
+		this->socket->disconnectFromServer();
 	}
 }
 
@@ -121,7 +123,7 @@ void IpcClient::onError(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError error) const {
 	qCCritical(logIpc) << "Socket Error" << error;
 }
 
-int IpcClient::connect(const QString& id, const std::function<void(IpcClient& client)>& callback) {
+int IpcClient::connect(const QString& id, const std::function<int(IpcClient& client)>& callback) {
 	auto path = QsPaths::ipcPath(id);
 	auto client = IpcClient(path);
 	qCDebug(logIpc) << "Connecting to instance" << id << "at" << path;
@@ -130,8 +132,9 @@ int IpcClient::connect(const QString& id, const std::function<void(IpcClient& cl
 	if (!client.isConnected()) return -1;
 	qCDebug(logIpc) << "Connected.";
 
-	callback(client);
-	return 0;
+	// What the command made of its answer is what qs exits with, so a reply
+	// lost on the way is told apart from one that came.
+	return callback(client);
 }
 
 void IpcKillCommand::exec(IpcServerConnection* /*unused*/) {
diff --git a/src/ipc/ipc.hpp b/src/ipc/ipc.hpp
index ad46afb..1bd5ed0 100644
--- a/src/ipc/ipc.hpp
+++ b/src/ipc/ipc.hpp
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ public:
 	}
 
 	[[nodiscard]] static int
-	connect(const QString& id, const std::function<void(IpcClient& client)>& callback);
+	connect(const QString& id, const std::function<int(IpcClient& client)>& callback);
 
 	// public for access by nonlocal handlers
 	QLocalSocket socket;
diff --git a/src/launch/command.cpp b/src/launch/command.cpp
index 6ec1a3f..3698556 100644
--- a/src/launch/command.cpp
+++ b/src/launch/command.cpp
@@ -435,6 +435,7 @@ int killInstances(CommandState& cmd) {
 	return IpcClient::connect(instance.instance.instanceId, [&](IpcClient& client) {
 		client.kill();
 		qCInfo(logBare).noquote() << "Killed" << instance.instance.instanceId;
+		return 0;
 	});
 }
 
